// XFAIL(x86_64-macos): RT-CG-4: x86-64 addresses a frame's slots with 32-bit displacements: a frame of 2 GiB or more cannot be assembled (open)
// XFAIL(x86_64-linux): RT-CG-4: x86-64 addresses a frame's slots with 32-bit displacements: a frame of 2 GiB or more cannot be assembled (open)
// (0.30.1) A function whose frame is larger than the stack faults on the
// guard page as it is entered, before it writes anything: a frame of a
// page or more is probed page by page, top to bottom (rustc's stack
// clash protection). Here the large local, 2^59 bytes (a type that
// fits), is in a branch not taken. Before, the frame moved sp past the
// address space's bottom and, through arm64's top-byte-ignore, onto the
// caller's own frame: the program went on writing over it and exited 0,
// its output lost.
// EXPECT: before
// EXIT: 139
#[inline(never)]
fn big(n: usize) {
    if n > 5 {
        let a = [0u8; 1usize << 59];
        println("{}", a[n]);
    }
    println("inside");
}

fn main() {
    let n = std::env::args().count();
    println("before");
    big(n);
    println("after");
}
